text:
Update; I got the keys to go 2 and what a difference it makes, much better than the previous one. There are actual keys, which make typing much easier and better. It got a screenshot key, as well as the smiley key. It's extremely light weight and portable, it's exactly what I was looking for.

Key to go, original one;
You'd think for the price this keyboard would offer an amazing typing experience but it doesn't. It is harsh on the fingers. I am female with carpel tunnel and let me tell you, 30 minutes typing on this keyboard and my fingers were stiff and in pain. As another reviewer said, it simply is no good...I have to press down really hard for the keys to register, or I have to double tap it. It is lightweight and waterproof (Altough how waterproof is something I have not been willing to test) and it looks adorable but the end results leave much to be desired and I wish I had returned it when I had the chance. I only bought it because I love my k380 and wanted something more portable...but I rather just carry the extra weight than endure the pain of typing on this one. Get the K380, it's much better and smoother. It's battery life is very good though, charge it only one a month...then again I don't really use it.

